IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc32-related-1`

-- ccc32-tests-related-1.l4 -- tests for ccc32-related-1.l4 (1991 c. 43 s. 10 to 2015 c. 20 s. 28).
-- Every expected value is decided by reading the provision, and written beside the assertion. A failing assertion is a finding.
-- The days are made-up days (the commencement days are not in the sources); the arithmetic on them is calendar arithmetic done by hand.

§ `1991 c. 43 s. 10(1) -- the order continues until an order is made under section 672.54`

-- A listed kind of order, made under the old section, with no 672.54 order yet: "shall continue in force" -> JUST TRUE.
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(1) the order for detention continues in force` `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order under section 614 of the Criminal Code` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(1) the order for detention continues in force` `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order under section 615 of the Criminal Code` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(1) the order for detention continues in force` `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order under section 617 of the Criminal Code` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(1) the order for detention continues in force` `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order under section 200 of the National Defence Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(1) the order for detention continues in force` `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order under section 201 of the National Defence Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "until an order is made by a court or Review Board under section 672.54": once made, the text says the order no longer continues -> JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(1) the order for detention continues in force` `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order under section 614 of the Criminal Code` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An order of a kind the subsection does not name, or one not made under the old text: outside the wording -> NOTHING (never FALSE).
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(1) the order for detention continues in force` `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order of another kind` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(1) the order for detention continues in force` `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order under section 614 of the Criminal Code` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `1991 c. 43 s. 10(2) -- the Review Board's review within twelve months`

-- The section came into force on 1 January 2020 (a made-up day): the twelve months run to 1 January 2021 (the same day twelve months on).
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(2) the review was within twelve months after the coming into force` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 31 12 2019) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(2) the review was within twelve months after the coming into force` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(2) the review was within twelve months after the coming into force` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2021) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(2) the review was within twelve months after the coming into force` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 2 1 2021) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Coming into force on 29 February 2020: daydate's `add months` clamps to 28 February 2021 (a finding about the arithmetic, fork F2 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(2) the review was within twelve months after the coming into force` (Date 29 2 2020) (Date 28 2 2021) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(2) the review was within twelve months after the coming into force` (Date 29 2 2020) (Date 1 3 2021) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The duty as a regulative rule (a DEONTIC cannot be asserted: read these three results). Time counts in MONTHS here.
-- Expected: the review in month 11 -> FULFILLED; in month 12 (the deadline is inclusive) -> FULFILLED; the clock at month 13 with no review -> BREACH.
#TRACE `1991 c 43 s 10(2) the Review Board must review the case` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a Review Board` DOES `1991 c 43 s 10(2) review the case of a person detained in custody by virtue of an order of detention referred to in subsection (1)` AT 11

#TRACE `1991 c 43 s 10(2) the Review Board must review the case` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a Review Board` DOES `1991 c 43 s 10(2) review the case of a person detained in custody by virtue of an order of detention referred to in subsection (1)` AT 12

#TRACE `1991 c 43 s 10(2) the Review Board must review the case` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 13)

§ `1991 c. 43 s. 10(3) -- sections 672.5 to 672.85 apply to the review`

`ccc32 test section 672.5` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 672.5, ""
`ccc32 test section 672.501` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 672.501, ""
`ccc32 test section 672.85` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 672.85, ""
`ccc32 test section 672.86` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 672.86, ""
`ccc32 test section 672.4` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 672.4, ""

-- Both ends of the range are in it, and so is a decimal section between them.
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(3) the section applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to the review` `ccc32 test section 672.5` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(3) the section applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to the review` `ccc32 test section 672.501` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(3) the section applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to the review` `ccc32 test section 672.85` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- One step outside either end, or not a review under subsection (2): not covered.
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(3) the section applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to the review` `ccc32 test section 672.86` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(3) the section applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to the review` `ccc32 test section 672.4` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(3) the section applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to the review` `ccc32 test section 672.5` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a) and (b): "as if".
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(3)(a) the review is treated as a review of a disposition conducted under section 672.81` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(3)(a) the review is treated as a review of a disposition conducted under section 672.81` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(3)(b) the warrant is treated as a disposition made under section 672.54` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(3)(b) the warrant is treated as a disposition made under section 672.54` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(3)(b) the warrant is treated as a disposition made under section 672.54` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)(c), (d) and (4) to (7) are shown repealed.
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(3)(c) and (d) as the text shows them` EQUALS "[Repealed, 2005, c. 22, s. 43]"
#ASSERT `1991 c 43 s 10(4) to (7) as the text shows them` EQUALS "[Repealed, 2005, c. 22, s. 43]"

§ `2004 c. 12 ss. 22 and 23 -- the references read as`

#ASSERT `2004 c 12 s 22 the reference is read as referring to` `2004 c 12 s 22 the reference in subsection 82(1) to Bill C-15, as it applies to subsections 82(2) and (4)` EQUALS JUST "Bill C-15A, which resulted from the division of Bill C-15 and has the same title"
#ASSERT `2004 c 12 s 22 the reference is read as referring to` `2004 c 12 s 22 the reference in subsection 82(2) to section 25 of the other Act` EQUALS JUST "section 16 of Bill C-15A"
#ASSERT `2004 c 12 s 22 the reference is read as referring to` `2004 c 12 s 22 the reference in subsection 82(4) to section 62 of the other Act` EQUALS JUST "section 52 of Bill C-15A"
#ASSERT `2004 c 12 s 22 the reference is read as referring to` `2004 c 12 s 22 another reference in section 82` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2004 c 12 s 23 the reference is read as referring to` `2004 c 12 s 23 the reference in subsection 82(1) to Bill C-15, as it applies to subsection 82(3)` EQUALS JUST "Bill C-10A, which resulted from the division of Bill C-10 and is entitled An Act to amend the Criminal Code (firearms) and the Firearms Act"
#ASSERT `2004 c 12 s 23 the reference is read as referring to` `2004 c 12 s 23 the reference in subsection 82(3) to section 32 of the other Act` EQUALS JUST "section 8 of Bill C-10A"
#ASSERT `2004 c 12 s 23 the reference is read as referring to` `2004 c 12 s 23 another reference in section 82` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `2009 c. 29 s. 5 -- charged AFTER the day`

-- 2009 c 29 s 5: the day is 2020-03-15; the text says "charged after the day": on the day itself is NOT after.
#ASSERT `2009 c 29 s 5 the person is within the limit on subsections 719(3) to (3.4)` (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 14 3 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `2009 c 29 s 5 the person is within the limit on subsections 719(3) to (3.4)` (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 15 3 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `2009 c 29 s 5 the person is within the limit on subsections 719(3) to (3.4)` (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 16 3 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE


§ `2011 c. 2 s. 7 -- applications under section 745.6`

-- (1) both limbs -> the Code as it read before governs; either missing -> not covered.
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(1) the application is dealt with and disposed of under the Code as it read immediately before that day` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(1) the application is dealt with and disposed of under the Code as it read immediately before that day` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(1) the application is dealt with and disposed of under the Code as it read immediately before that day` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) determination on 15 March 2020: two years on is 15 March 2022; the window is 16 March 2022 to 11 September 2022 (180 days after 15 March 2022).
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(2) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 15 3 2022) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(2) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 16 3 2022) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(2) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 11 9 2022) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(2) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 12 9 2022) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(2) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` FALSE TRUE (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 16 3 2022) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(2) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` TRUE FALSE (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 16 3 2022) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) a time set that ends on 1 June 2021: the window is 2 June 2021 to 28 November 2021.
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(3) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2021) (Date 1 6 2021) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(3) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2021) (Date 2 6 2021) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(3) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2021) (Date 28 11 2021) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(3) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2021) (Date 29 11 2021) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(3) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 6 2021) (Date 2 6 2021) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2011 c 2 s 7(3) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 6 2021) (Date 2 6 2021) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `2012 c. 1 ss. 163(a) and 165(b) -- a record suspension reference is also a pardon reference`

`ccc32 test paragraph 672.35(c)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 672.35, "(c)"
`ccc32 test subsection 750(4)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 750, "(4)"
`ccc32 test subsection 490.011(1)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 490.011, "(1)"
`ccc32 test paragraph 672.35(a)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 672.35, "(a)"

#ASSERT `2012 c 1 s 163(a) the reference to an application for a record suspension is also a reference to an application for a pardon` `ccc32 test paragraph 672.35(c)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2012 c 1 s 163(a) the reference to an application for a record suspension is also a reference to an application for a pardon` `ccc32 test subsection 750(4)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A provision the paragraph does not list; a pardon application already finally disposed of: not covered.
#ASSERT `2012 c 1 s 163(a) the reference to an application for a record suspension is also a reference to an application for a pardon` `ccc32 test paragraph 672.35(a)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2012 c 1 s 163(a) the reference to an application for a record suspension is also a reference to an application for a pardon` `ccc32 test paragraph 672.35(c)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2012 c 1 s 163(a) the reference to an application for a record suspension is also a reference to an application for a pardon` `ccc32 test paragraph 672.35(c)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2012 c 1 s 165(b) the reference to a record suspension is also a reference to a pardon` `ccc32 test subsection 490.011(1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2012 c 1 s 165(b) the reference to a record suspension is also a reference to a pardon` `ccc32 test paragraph 672.35(c)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2012 c 1 s 165(b) the reference to a record suspension is also a reference to a pardon` `ccc32 test subsection 490.011(1)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2012 c 1 s 165(b) the reference to a record suspension is also a reference to a pardon` `ccc32 test subsection 490.011(1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `2015 c. 13 ss. 37 to 44`

-- 2015 c 13 s 37: the day is 2020-03-15; the window is the day itself and the next 14 days, that is up to 2020-03-29.
#ASSERT `2015 c 13 s 37 subsection 278.3(5) as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the hearing` (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 14 3 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `2015 c 13 s 37 subsection 278.3(5) as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the hearing` (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 15 3 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2015 c 13 s 37 subsection 278.3(5) as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the hearing` (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 29 3 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2015 c 13 s 37 subsection 278.3(5) as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the hearing` (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 30 3 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `2015 c 13 s 37 subsection 278.3(5) as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the hearing` (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 15 3 2020) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING


-- 2015 c 13 s 38: the day is 2020-03-15; made before it -> continues to apply; on or after it -> NOT COVERED (never FALSE).
#ASSERT `2015 c 13 s 38 section 380.3 as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the request for restitution` (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 14 3 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2015 c 13 s 38 section 380.3 as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the request for restitution` (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 15 3 2020) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2015 c 13 s 38 section 380.3 as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the request for restitution` (Date 15 3 2020) (Date 16 3 2020) EQUALS NOTHING


-- 2015 c 13 s 39: the day is 2020-03-15; made before it -> continues to apply; on or after it -> NOT COVERED (never FALSE).
